ck to see a cheap flop. Q♣ 8♣ has decent implied odds: if the flop comes with clubs, high cards, or connected boards, we can play aggressively. If not, we can fold cheaply.  \n\nRaising to 200 isn\'t terrible, but given we\'re already in the lead and this is hand #18 of 20, preserving chip advantage with smart, low-risk plays is wise. There\'s no need to gamble unnecessarily.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
